    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n79588" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρθέν-ιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ος</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Pi.
			<u>P.</u>
			12.9
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			E.
			<u>Ph.</u>
			224
		</span></i> (lyr.) :—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of a
				maiden, maidenly</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λῦσε δὲ παρθενίην ζώνην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					11.245
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄαροι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Th.</u>
					205
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔρως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Anacr.
					13
				</span></i>
			A ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεφαλαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
				</span></i>
			 l.c. ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἷμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					215
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χλιδά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					224
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. θύραι</span>”
				<i>of the temple of the Virgin Goddess,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					AP
					6.202
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Leon.
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρθένιον βλέπειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Anacr.
					4
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. αὐλός</span>, 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐλός</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				1.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρθένιος, ὁ</span>, <i>the son of an unmarried girl</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				16.180
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρθενία ὠδίς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>O.</u>
					6.31
				</span></i>
			 ; but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ἀνήρ</span> the husband
				<i>of maidenhood, first</i> husband, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Pomp.</u>
				74
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> metaph.,
				<i>pure, undefiled</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Π.
			φρέαρ</span>, name of a well, <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Cer.</u>
				99
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. μύρτα</span>, of
			<i>white</i> myrtle-berries, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				1099
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. γαῖα</span>, =
			<i>Samia terra</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Al.</u>
				149
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Π., ὁ </span>(sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήν</span>), a month in Elis, Sch. <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				3.35
			</span></i>.</div>
